      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page (from [[write-journal]]) describes a mechanism that provides transactional safety for file writes in the Grimoire system. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core function**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it first journals (records in memory) the prior state of that file \u2014 either its previous content if it existed, or a note that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n**Rollback capability**: If an agent run fails for any reason (hitting a turn cap, encountering an unrecoverable error, or all writes being denied), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order \u2014 restoring previously existing files to their old state and deleting any newly created files.\n\n**All-or-nothing semantics**: This approach gives each run transactional \u0022all-or-nothing\u0022 semantics for its writes without requiring a database; the in-memory journal itself acts as the transaction log for the duration of one run.\n\n**Query agent note**: The Query agent (like the one you\u0027re using now) never uses the journal\u0027s rollback path since it has no write tool at all \u2014 the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library but is only populated by agents that actually write.",
      "input_tokens": 5572,
